<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Temwen Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Temwen Island is a small island off the eastern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pohnpei">Pohnpei</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federated-states-of-micronesia">Federated States of Micronesia</a>. On the reef beside it lies Nan Madol, a complex of nearly a hundred artificial islets built of basalt columns and coral, which served as the ceremonial and political centre of the Saudeleur dynasty. Nan Madol was inscribed as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 2016.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/temwen-island.jpg" alt="Temwen Island" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CT Snow from Hsinchu, Taiwan · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nan_Madol_5.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
